==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*sitjaną}}, from {{m|gem-pro||*set-}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*sed-||sit}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|sitta}} ({{cog|fy|sitte}}), {{cog|goh|sizzen}} ({{cog|de|sitzen}}), {{cog|osx|sittian}}, {{cog|nl|zitten}}, {{cog|non|sitja}} ({{cog|is|sitja}}, {{cog|fo|sita}}, {{cog|sv|sitta}}), {{cog|got|𐍃𐌹𐍄𐌰𐌽}}. The {{etyl|ine-pro|-}} root is also the source of {{cog|sa|सीदति}}, {{cog|xcl|նիստ||sitting}}, {{cog|sga|saidid}} ({{cog|ga|suigh}}), {{cog|grc|ἕζομαι}}, {{cog|la|sedeō}}, {{cog|cu|sc=Cyrs|сѣдѣти}} ({{cog|ru|сиде́ть}}).

